            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of 4-substituted pyrazole-3,5-diamines via Suzuki-Miyaura coupling and iron-catalyzed reduction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10200-10211</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02373a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A general and efficient synthesis of 4-substituted-1H-pyrazole-3,5-diamines was developed to access derivatives with an aryl, heteroaryl, or styryl group, which are otherwise relatively difficult to prepare. The first step is based on the Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction utilizing the XPhos Pd G2 precatalyst. The coupling reactions of 4-bromo-3,5-dinitro-1H-pyrazole with the electron-rich/deficient or sterically demanding boronic acids enabled the production of the corresponding dinitropyrazoles. The subsequent iron-catalyzed reduction of both nitro groups with hydrazine hydrate accomplished the synthesis. The additional demethylation of the 4-methoxystyryl derivative allowed the production of the carboanalog of CAN508 reported as a selective CDK9 inhibitor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
